From 527903bec18e3b62b7efcfe3d5c31ad49de42b55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 01:12:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prerender real page HTML so crawlers stop reading stale
 metadata

The site ships as a Vite SPA with an empty <div id="root">. The existing
prerender step baked per-route meta tags but never any body, so every URL
returned ~4KB of head and nothing else. Crawlers that do not execute JS, and
the retrieval layers behind AI answer engines, had only the meta description to
quote. Perplexity's answer for "Axiom Specialty" was built from the privacy
policy plus a California licence record for an unrelated company of the same
name, and still describes the appetite as professional services, wording
retired from the site months ago but still cached against dead URLs.

- scripts/prerender-seo.mjs now renders each route in headless Chromium and
  writes the resulting DOM to disk. Home goes from 0 to ~2,800 characters of
  readable text, the AI liability page to ~11,400. The SPA still boots and
  replaces the markup on load; client-side navigation and direct hits produce
  identical DOM.
- Reclaim pages at /contact, /brokerages, /blog and /blog/post-0000. All four
  are indexed with the old "professional services firms" description and all
  four now 404, so the stale copy would sit there until it aged out. Each now
  serves the current description with a canonical to its live replacement.
- Organization schema gains a disambiguatingDescription separating this company
  from the similarly named agency licensed in Texas and California, plus
  founder, founding date, address, areaServed, knowsAbout and the AI liability
  service with its actual audience.
- public/llms.txt states the current facts in plain text, including an explicit
  list of the wrong claims circulating in third-party records.
- robots.txt names the AI crawlers explicitly rather than relying on wildcard.
- Sitemap gains lastmod.
- CI installs Chromium and sets PRERENDER_REQUIRE_RENDER=1, so a Chromium
  failure fails the build instead of silently republishing empty pages.

docs/ is left to the build workflow to regenerate.
---
 .github/workflows/build-docs.yml |   9 ++
 index.html                       |  76 +++++++++-
 package-lock.json                |  66 ++++++---
 package.json                     |   1 +
 public/llms.txt                  |  86 +++++++++++
 public/robots.txt                |  56 +++++++
 scripts/prerender-seo.mjs        | 245 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/content/seo.json             |  19 +++
 8 files changed, 503 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 public/llms.txt

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build-docs.yml b/.github/workflows/build-docs.yml
index 9441049..8b804fa 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build-docs.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build-docs.yml
@@ -2,6 +2,11 @@
 # changes land on main. This is what makes CMS edits publish: Pages CMS commits a
 # Markdown post, this workflow rebuilds docs/ and commits it back, and the live
 # site updates without anyone running a build locally.
+#
+# The build prerenders every route in headless Chromium, so the committed HTML
+# carries the real page text rather than an empty SPA shell. That is what
+# crawlers and AI answer engines read. PRERENDER_REQUIRE_RENDER=1 makes the
+# build fail if Chromium cannot run, rather than quietly publishing empty pages.
 name: Build docs
 
 on:
@@ -28,7 +33,11 @@ jobs:
           node-version: 20
           cache: npm
       - run: npm ci
+      - name: Install Chromium for prerendering
+        run: npx playwright install --with-deps chromium
       - run: npm run build
+        env:
+          PRERENDER_REQUIRE_RENDER: "1"
       - name: Commit rebuilt docs
         run: |
           git config user.name "github-actions[bot]"
